@{
    ViewBag.Title = "Testing Canvas Elements, Automating Canvas - Demo Page";
}

<div id="content">
    <!--  CONTENT   -->
    <div id="page-header" class="page-demo">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="span12 whitebg">
                <h1>Demo <span>Canvas</span> with Ui.Vision RPA</h1>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">


        <div class="span12">



            <p>
                The Selenium IDE ClickAt command and the <em>Ui.Vision RPA</em> image search commands are a good solution for automating
                and visual UI testing canvas element. VisualSearch can see inside the canvas, and ClickAt can
                click inside.
            </p> 
            <p>The DemoCanvas macro visits two <em>external</em> websites, and checks their canvas. Then it checks the embedded Google map below.</p>
            <p>
                <ul>
                    <li><a href="http://literallycanvas.com/">LiterallyCanvas</a> - Drawing app</li>
                    <li><a href="https://www.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/example/queryrenderedfeatures-around-point/">Mapbox</a> - Embedded map, macro finds and click Wyoming</li>
                 </ul>


            </p>
            <h3 id="maps">Google Maps Canvas Demo</h3>
            <p>
                <div class="mapouter">
                    <div class="gmap_canvas"><iframe width="600" height="500" id="gmap_canvas" src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=london&t=&z=13&ie=UTF8&iwloc=&output=embed" frameborder="0" scrolling="no" marginheight="0" marginwidth="0"></iframe><a href="https://www.pureblack.de">webdesign: pureblack.de</a></div>
                    <style>
                        .mapouter {
                            text-align: right;
                            height: 500px;
                            width: 600px;
                        }

                        .gmap_canvas {
                            overflow: hidden;
                            background: none !important;
                            height: 500px;
                            width: 600px;
                        }
                    </style>
                </div>

            </p>

        </div>
    </div>
</div>
